{
  "sn47.10:0.1": "Linked Discourses 47.10 ",
  "sn47.10:0.2": "1. In Ambapālī’s Mango Grove ",
  "sn47.10:0.3": "The Nuns’ Quarters ",
  "sn47.10:1.1": "Then Venerable Ānanda robed up in the morning and, taking his bowl and robe, went to the nuns’ quarters, and sat down on the seat spread out. ",
  "sn47.10:1.2": "Then several nuns went up to Venerable Ānanda bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him: ",
  "sn47.10:2.1": "“Honorable Ānanda, several nuns meditate with their minds firmly established in the four kinds of mindfulness meditation. They have realized a higher distinction than they had before.” ",
  "sn47.10:2.2": "“That’s how it is, sisters! That’s how it is, sisters! ",
  "sn47.10:2.3": "Any monk or nun who meditates with their mind firmly established in the four kinds of mindfulness meditation can expect to ",
  "sn47.10:2.4": "realize a higher distinction than they had before.” ",
  "sn47.10:3.1": "Then Ānanda educated, encouraged, fired up, and inspired those nuns with a Dhamma talk, after which he rose from his seat and left. ",
  "sn47.10:3.2": "Then Ānanda wandered for alms in Sāvatthī. After the meal, on his return from almsround, he went to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and told him what had happened. ",
  "sn47.10:4.1": "",
